1
00:00:02,950 --> 00:00:06,037
The most famous view in the American West!

2
00:00:06,037 --> 00:00:09,271
The spot where Forrest Gump stopped running.

3
00:00:09,271 --> 00:00:12,064
A river looping a thousand feet below.

4
00:00:12,064 --> 00:00:16,400
And three miles of gravel switchbacks, straight up a cliff!

5
00:00:17,350 --> 00:00:23,245
This is Monument Valley to the Moki Dugway: about 50 miles on the Utah-Arizona border.

6
00:00:23,245 --> 00:00:26,810
Stick around till the end for the full trip planner!

7
00:00:27,760 --> 00:00:28,915
Here's the plan!

8
00:00:28,915 --> 00:00:38,300
We start in Monument Valley, then Forrest Gump Point, Mexican Hat and the Goosenecks, and we finish at the top of the Moki Dugway!

9
00:00:39,250 --> 00:00:42,848
We're starting in Monument Valley Navajo Tribal Park!

10
00:00:42,848 --> 00:00:47,396
The Mittens and Merrick Butte have starred in Westerns for decades.

11
00:00:47,396 --> 00:00:52,420
Drive the 17-mile Valley Drive, or book a Navajo-guided tour to go deeper.

12
00:00:53,370 --> 00:00:54,873
North on US 163.

13
00:00:54,873 --> 00:00:58,160
Don't forget to look in the mirror!

14
00:00:59,110 --> 00:01:01,201
Pull over at Forrest Gump Point!

15
00:01:01,201 --> 00:01:07,867
This is where Forrest finally stopped running, with Monument Valley lined up behind him down the road.

16
00:01:07,867 --> 00:01:10,350
Get your photo, but watch for traffic!

17
00:01:11,300 --> 00:01:15,930
Down to the San Juan River, and the little town of Mexican Hat!

18
00:01:16,880 --> 00:01:23,440
Welcome to Mexican Hat, named after a rock just outside town that looks exactly like a giant sombrero!

19
00:01:24,390 --> 00:01:27,030
Out across the mesa to the edge of the Goosenecks!

20
00:01:27,990 --> 00:01:30,131
This is Goosenecks State Park!

21
00:01:30,131 --> 00:01:39,980
The San Juan River twists through these tight loops a thousand feet below you, winding more than six miles just to move a mile and a half!

22
00:01:40,930 --> 00:01:45,520
North on Highway 261, straight toward a wall of cliffs.

23
00:01:45,520 --> 00:01:47,440
Where does the road go?

24
00:01:48,390 --> 00:01:51,653
And the grand finale, the Moki Dugway!

25
00:01:51,653 --> 00:01:59,383
About three miles of steep gravel switchbacks, climbing over a thousand feet up the cliff.

26
00:01:59,383 --> 00:02:03,676
At the top, look back over the Valley of the Gods.

27
00:02:03,676 --> 00:02:04,020
Wow!

28
00:02:04,970 --> 00:02:06,527
And that's the drive!

29
00:02:06,527 --> 00:02:11,420
About 50 miles from Monument Valley to the top of the Moki Dugway.

30
00:02:12,370 --> 00:02:15,748
Here's your trip planner, everything in one place.

31
00:02:15,748 --> 00:02:17,640
Pause and grab a screenshot!

32
00:02:20,870 --> 00:02:22,342
Thanks for riding along!

33
00:02:22,342 --> 00:02:27,740
Subscribe to Road Trip Atlas for more Utah road trips, and I'll see you on the next one!
